msgid "A RESOURCE (the set, the handle a person stamps, cites and opens) has ONE OF ITS FILES (E.D. 2026-09-30, «la risorsa e i suoi file»). The edge — not the file — carries in its \\`attributes\\` the ROLE (\\`entry\\_point\\`: the file a reader opens first, e.g. the obj or tileset.json; \\`member\\`: a file the entry point calls, e.g. the mtl and the textures) and the PATH relative to the entry point's location (\\`path\\`, e.g. 'textures/T\\_OB\\_PODIO\\_LOD1.jpg'), because the same file sits in N resources under N different paths. With ONE file the edge is implicit and not written: the ResourceNode's own url and checksum are that file."
msgstr ""

